last question today david do you believe  that people whose  hobby is politics actually get anything  done  politically this is a i want to be  careful in how i talk about this because  if i were to say people who just follow  politics  as a hobby and source of entertainment  don't get a damn thing done  i think it would potentially be  disaffecting to many people  my view is that and we we've done  interviews on this before and it's an  important question we've talked about it  with rachel bittikoffer and with other  people  political hobbyists don't get much done  themselves if they only remain political  hobbyists  however they may number one  by sharing information on social media  get  other people to go beyond being merely  political hobbyists and being  actual political activists who get  things done but for many people being a  political hobbyist  is the entry path into being more of an  activist someone who actually calls  elected officials organizes  uh does voter registration volunteers  for candidates etc  etc etc so if the question  you it's the devil isn't how you ask the  devil's in the details of the question  do people who never go beyond merely  following politics like entertainment  help to achieve  change very very little hopefully they  at least vote not all political  hobbyists even vote but to the extent  that they do voting is important  if the question is can being a political  hobbyist  lead to being someone that actually does  achieve  change by becoming an organizer or  someone who volunteers for campaigns or  whatever else the answer is absolutely  yes and i know tons of people and many  are in our audience  who started just by watching shows shows  like this and and other shows  and voted but then eventually really  became engaged and i can think of people  in lots of different parts of the  country where  that's the case so what is important is  not to  dismiss those who are interested in  politics  and follow it as a hobby as people who  can never get anything done  it's a matter of encouraging them to get  more involved  and there are so many ways that that can  be done either running for something at  the local level volunteering  for a local state or national election  and doing phone banking and text banking  and all these different things  people who one other thing right now  be the candidate that raises more money  in a race is more likely to win it's not  a hundred percent it's not correlated at  one  but there's a correlation between  raising more money and being able to uh  and ultimately winning  if you become a political hobbyist and  you donate money  you are also involved in a way that  materially affects outcomes  i wish that it wasn't the case that our  political system depended on money in  that way  it's a disgusting corrosive system that  must be changed  but if you're not only a political  hobbyist but someone who donates  to candidates that you believe in you  are also having an impact and we know  that and there's a reason that raising  money is so important and and such a  important factor in signaling who might  actually win an election  so let's embrace the political hobbyists  to do more  rather than writing them off as people  who make no difference and the truth is  most people  in my audience are political hobbyists  some percentage of them  are more than that and hopefully we can  encourage that number  to grow even further let me know your  thoughts we also  have a great bonus show for you today  the bonus show is only exclusively for  our  website members and patreon  donors you can sign up at joinpakman.com  you can sign up at patreon.com david  pakman show either way you'll get  instant access to the bonus show  why not do it before april is gone you  have just  hours to go i'll see you then
 

